  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLACSO 2018-2022</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CLACSO 2018-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Strengthening and enhancing the research capacities of CLACSO institutional network in priority fields of social sciences and humanities, increasing the opportunities for the development of high-quality academic production, by means of peers evaluation processes.

2. Contributing to develop institutional synergies that encourage the tasks of quality and relevance social research that different universities conduct and think tanks in Latin America and the Caribbean.

3. Promoting programs of applied research that allow knowledge production to processes of democratic social innovation in line with the challenges that open in the region to fulfill the Sustainable Development Objectives and to the 2030 Agenda.

4. Enhancing the research opportunities and the creation of scientific communities in those Latin American and Caribbean countries where social sciences and humanities had less relative development.

5. Promoting institutional strategies that contribute to the building of bridges between social research and public policies oriented towards democratic social innovation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Det regionala latinamerikanska och karibiska samh&#xe4;llsvetenskapliga forskningsr&#xe5;det CLACSO har ans&#xf6;kt om medel fr&#xe5;n Sida p&#xe5; 30 miljoner kronor f&#xf6;r att implementera programmet &quot;Forskning f&#xf6;r social och demokratisk innovation&quot; &#xf6;ver hela regionen under perioden juli 2018 till juni 2021.

Insatsen syftar till att st&#xe4;rka och fr&#xe4;mja forskningskapacitet hos CLACSOs institutionella medlemmar - som best&#xe5;r av universitetsinstitutioner och tankesmedjor &#xf6;ver hela kontinenten - samt att fr&#xe4;mja att forskningsresultat anv&#xe4;nds i innovationsprocesser f&#xf6;r samh&#xe4;llsf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring. Detta sker genom utlysningar f&#xf6;r forskningsmedel, st&#xf6;d till regionala tematiska arbetsgrupper som integrerar forskare och andra sektorer av samh&#xe4;llet, samt forskarskolor och kurser f&#xf6;r att st&#xe4;rka medlemsinstitutionernas forskarutbildning. Programmet prioriterar s&#xe4;rskilt l&#xe4;nder i regionen d&#xe4;r samh&#xe4;llsvetenskaplig forskning &#xe4;r mindre utvecklad, till exempel Central America, Bolivia, Paraguay och Haiti.

CLACSOs totala budget &#xe4;r f&#xf6;r n&#xe4;rvarande p&#xe5; omkring 5 miljoner US dollar per &#xe5;r (omkring h&#xe4;lften av detta &#xe4;r motfinansiering fr&#xe5;n medlemsinstitutionerna), inklusive st&#xf6;det fr&#xe5;n Sida. De 30 miljoner kronor som de s&#xf6;ker fr&#xe5;n Sida g&#xe4;ller n&#xe5;gra av komponenterna i CLACSOs tre&#xe5;rsplan juli 2018 - juni 2021, 10 miljoner kronor per &#xe5;r under tre &#xe5;r. Insatsen &#xe4;r ett utfasningsst&#xf6;d f&#xf6;r att underl&#xe4;tta CLACSOs &#xf6;verg&#xe5;ng till finansiellt oberoende efter ett m&#xe5;ng&#xe5;rigt st&#xf6;d fr&#xe5;n Sida.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The regional Latin American and Caribbean social science research council CLACSO has applied for funding from Sida on 30 million SEK to implement the programme &quot;Research for social and democratic innovation&quot; over the whole region during the period July 2018 to June 2021.

The intervention intends to strengthen and promote research capacity within CLACSO&apos;s institutional members - consisting of university institutions and think thanks over the whole continent - as well as promote the use of research results in innovation processes for social change. This will be accomplished through open calls for research grants, support to regional thematic working groups integrating researchers and other sectors of society, as well as research training schools and courses in order to strengthen the member institutions&apos; research training. The programme especially prioritizes countries in the region where social science research is less developed, for example Central America, Bolivia, Paraguay and Haiti.

CLACSO&apos;s total budget is approximately USD 5 million a year (about half of it contributions in kind from the member institutions), including the Sida support. The SEK 30 million applied from Sida will cover some of the components in the three years plan July 2018 - June 2021, SEK 10 million a year during three years. The intervention is a phasing-out support to facilitate CLACSO&apos;s transition to financial independence after many years of Sida support.</narrative>
  </description>
